      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "stiffness; spasms; startle; anti-GAD antibody; EMG showing continuous motor unit activity; response to benzodiazepines and baclofen",
      "quote": "Furthermore, characteristic symptoms and laboratory findings also indicated stiff person syndrome. These findings suggested that his symptoms could be attributed to paraneoplastic neurological syndrome associated with the mediastinal tumor. Surface electromyography of the right quadriceps muscle and hamstrings at rest showed continuous motor unit activity. These symptoms were not affected by initial treatment with steroids, but they were improved by benzodiazepine and baclofen treatment.",
